"comparison": "Both GS and BAC define the composition of Total Loss-Absorbing Capacity (TLAC) as including equity and eligible long-term unsecured debt issued by the parent holding company with a remaining maturity of at least one year. GS explicitly states TLAC includes common and preferred stock plus eligible long-term debt, while BAC defines TLAC as consisting of Tier 1 capital and eligible long-term debt issued directly by the Corporation. Both disclosures specify that eligible long-term debt must be unsecured with a remaining maturity of at least one year.",
